Spoilers of obvious content...

(There has got to be an easier way to get a ^L in Emacs than rebinding
 C-L to self-insert-command!)

This is the easy thing: sacrifice on it a few times.  Each time, you'll either
lose luck or change the altar.  The hard thing to do is convert yourself.
It's rumored to be possible to do this by sacrificing as above while your
god is angry, but I've never done it; I think this advice is bogus. 
Sacrificing a unicorn of your own alignment seems to work reliably, though.

Recommendation: convert the neutral one.  Lawfuls are good for holy water.
If any one of them is near a sink, take that one, though.

